<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">How to Download YouTube Videos on Mobile</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Downloading YouTube videos on your phone is easier than ever. Whether you use an iPhone, iPad, or Android device, you can save public YouTube videos directly in your browser without installing any app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 1: Copy the YouTube video URL</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Open the YouTube app or website, tap the <strong>Share</strong> button, and choose <strong>Copy link</strong>. The URL should look like <code>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 2: Open ClipVault in your mobile browser</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Go to <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a> in Safari, Chrome, or any browser. The site is mobile-friendly and loads quickly.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 3: Paste the URL and choose a format</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Paste the copied link into the input box, solve the captcha, and tap <strong>Get Video</strong>. After a few seconds, you will see a list of available formats such as MP4 video and MP3 audio. Pick the one that fits your device and storage.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 4: Download the file</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Tap the format you want. On most phones, the file will download to your <strong>Downloads</strong> folder or prompt you to save it. You can move the video to your Photos or Files app afterward.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Tips for a smooth mobile download</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Use a stable Wi-Fi connection to avoid interruptions.</li>
        <li>Choose a lower resolution if your storage is limited.</li>
        <li>Use headphones or mobile data carefully if the video is large.</li>
        <li>Only download content you created, own, or have permission to use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Important copyright reminder</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">YouTube's Terms of Service restrict downloading unless a download button is provided or you have permission. Use this guide for your own videos, public domain content, or Creative Commons works. See our <a href="/content-policy" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline">Content Policy</a> for more.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
